{"id": "y0053", "pool": "know-longtail", "n_q_chunks": 2, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Judaism is a monothe ist religion that dates back thousands of years. It's based on the belief in one God and the teachings found in the He brew Bible, also known as the Old Testament. Jud aism has many traditions and practices, including prayer, holiday celebration s, and observ ance of religious laws. There are different branches of Ju daism, such as Or thodox, Conservative, Re form, and Reform, each with its own interpretations of Jewish law and practice s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 27, "carrier_ended": null}
