{"id": "y0165", "pool": "know-longtail", "n_q_chunks": 3, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Elrond Hubbard is a fictional character in J.R.R. To lkein's Middle-earth stories, so he does not have a religion like a real person would. However, his beliefs are deeply rooted in the lore of Middle-earth. He follows the ancient traditions and wisdom passed down through the Elf kin, particularly the teachings of Galad ril and Celeborn. His faith revolve s around living in harmony with nature, honor ing ancient ways, and maintaining balance between light and darkness. While there isn't a specific named religion for him, he embodies the spiritual values of the Elves—a blend of reverence for life, respect for history, and a deep connection to the world around them.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
