{"id": "y1037", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 20, "onset_chunk": 19, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So if a patient cuts a peripheral motor nerve in their wrist and the nerve does not regenerate after about six months, the muscles it normally innervates will show signs of atro phy. When a nerve is cut or damaged, the muscle s it controls can no longer receive signals from the brain to contract. Over time, without stimulation, these muscles start to waste away because they are not being used properly. This process is known as muscle atrophy. Spastic paralysis involves involuntary muscle spasms, which would not typically occur with just a cut nerve. Fl acid paraly sis describes the loss of muscle tone but doesn't specifically indicate the long-term tissue damage seen over months. Con tracture refers to stiffening due to prolonged immobility, which may happen later, but the primary change after six months without re generation is atro phy.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 44, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1045", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 35, "onset_chunk": 35, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C. The tax is constitutional because the Su premacy Clause validate s laws enacted by Congress. That' s right, this tax would be considered constitutional under the Supremacy Clause of the Constitution. The Supremacy Clause establishes that federal law takes precedence over state laws when there is a conflict. Since Congress has the authority to regulate commerce among the states, including taxing goods sold in interstate commerce, it can impose such a tax even if the product is sold across state lines. Therefore, option C is correct.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 31, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "y1053", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The ductus art eriosus is a shunt that allows blood to bypass the lungs before birth. It connect s the pulmonary artery, which carries deoxygenated blood from the heart to the lungs, to the aorta, which carry es oxygen ated blood to the body. So it actually allows some of the blood coming from the right ventricle to go directly into the aorta instead of going through the lungs. That means the correct answer is C: pulmonary artery to the aorta.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 29, "carrier_ended": null}
